  "details": "As a VRC+ user, I would like to pick a custom icon, and be given the choice to *not* display it to other users except in cases where my nameplate would show up with icons-only mode:\n- when the other users have nameplates in icons-only mode\n- whenever my username is currently not displayed, for instance when it is too far from another user\nCurrently, this only seems to be achievable with the default icon (where the first 3 letters of the username become the icon).\nHere's my motivation for this ticket: Custom avatars are redundant with custom icons. I feel like there's no point in showing a picture of my avatar's face on my nameplate if I'm close to someone, and there's no point in showing a picture of my name if my username is already showing up in the nameplate.\nTherefore, in the current situation, I'd rather continue to use the default icon as a VRC+ user so that my nameplate displays without any icon.\nBut since I am subscribed to VRC+ anyways, I might aswell choose a custom icon to show up if my username does not show up in my nameplate.",
